Specification Reports

Description Reporting by category and by payee, over a date range or over many
Description years side by side.
Details
Details Every figure in a report is a total of postings. A report never reads a
Details stored total, so it cannot disagree with the register, and a correction
Details made in 2007 shows in a report run today without anything being
Details rebuilt.
Details
Details Amounts are shown with the display sign of the account, so income and
Details expenses are both positive and a reader does not have to hold the sign
Details convention in their head. See the display sign rule in Accounts.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Asking for a report
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Attributes ReportSpec
Description What was asked for.
| Attribute   | Type           | Default    |
| GroupBy     | ReportGrouping | Category   |
| From        | Date           | 2024-01-01 |
| To          | Date           | 2024-12-31 |
| Interval    | ReportInterval | Whole      |
| Depth       | Integer        | 0          |
| Detail      | ReportDetail   | AllCategories |
| Subtotals   | Boolean        | true       |
| ZeroRows    | Boolean        | false      |
| IncludeInvestmentActivity | Boolean | false  |
| QuickenSigns | Boolean     | false      |

DataType ReportGrouping
Description What the rows of the report are.
Examples: EnumerationValues
| Value    | Notes                                        |
| Category | One row per income or expense account        |
| Payee    | One row per payee                            |
| Account  | One row per real account, for a balance sheet |

DataType ReportInterval
Description What the columns of the report are.
Examples: EnumerationValues
| Value   | Notes                                       |
| Whole   | One column for the whole range              |
| Month   | One column per calendar month               |
| Quarter | One column per calendar quarter             |
| Year    | One column per year                         |
| FiscalYear | One column per fiscal year               |

DataType ReportDetail
Description How much of the category tree a report shows, which is the choice
Description offered on the report itself.
Details HighestOnly is the summary: one line for each category at the top of a
Details section, with everything below it rolled up into its figure. It is the
Details same report as Depth 1, under the name the window offers.
Details
Details AllCategories is the whole tree, each category indented one step further
Details than its parent so that a child reads as belonging to the line above it.
Details
Details Transactions is the whole tree with the transactions behind each figure
Details shown under it, which is the drill-down of every line at once rather
Details than one line at a time. See the drill-down section below.
Examples: EnumerationValues
| Value         | Notes                                                 |
| HighestOnly   | One line per category at the top of a section         |
| AllCategories | Every category, indented under its parent             |
| Transactions  | Every category, with the transactions behind each one |

Attributes ReportRow
Description One row of a single-column report.
| Attribute | Type        | Default |
| Account   | AccountPath |         |
| Level     | Integer     | 0       |
| Amount    | Money       | 0.00    |
| IsSubtotal | Boolean    | false   |

