Scenario A category report for one year
Description The tree is kept, with a subtotal on every placeholder, and income
Description and expenses both read as positive figures.
Given the chart of accounts is as previous
Given postings are as previous
When report run : ReportSpec Vertical
| GroupBy  | Category   |
| From     | 2024-01-01 |
| To       | 2024-12-31 |
| Interval | Whole      |
Then report rows are : ReportRow
| Account                | Level | Amount   | IsSubtotal |
| Income                 | 0     | 42025.00 | true       |
| Income:Interest        | 1     | 25.00    | false      |
| Income:Salary          | 1     | 42000.00 | false      |
| Expenses               | 0     | 960.00   | true       |
| Expenses:Auto          | 1     | 450.00   | true       |
| Expenses:Auto:Fuel     | 2     | 150.00   | false      |
| Expenses:Auto:Repairs  | 2     | 300.00   | false      |
| Expenses:Groceries     | 1     | 500.00   | false      |
| Expenses:Uncategorized | 1     | 10.00    | false      |
Then report total is : ReportTotal Vertical
| TotalIncome   | 42025.00 |
| TotalExpenses | 960.00   |
| Net           | 41065.00 |

Attributes ReportTotal
| Attribute     | Type  | Default |
| TotalIncome   | Money | 0.00    |
| TotalExpenses | Money | 0.00    |
| Net           | Money | 0.00    |

Scenario Quicken signs show expenses negative
Description The same report as above with QuickenSigns asked for, which is how
Description Quicken writes it: income positive, expenses negative. For reading
Description a figure against a Quicken report side by side, where having to
Description negate one column in your head is where mistakes come from.
Details The rule is uniform and has no special cases: a Quicken expense figure
Details is the negation of ours, every row, and that holds for a category whose
Details figure is a credit as well. Measured on the 2021 business report, where
Details Clear Out Balances reads 127.56 in Quicken and -127.56 here, and
Details Groceries reads -12,129.60 there and 12,129.60 here.
Details
Details The net does not move. Only the sign of the expenses figure does, so
Details the net is income plus expenses in this mode and income minus expenses
Details in the other, and both come to the same number.
Details
Details Income is untouched because the two conventions already agree on it.
Details Payee reports keep the other convention whatever this is set to: a
Details payee report sums a payee's income and expense postings into one
Details figure, so a payee with both has no sensible sign here, and flipping it
Details would make the number meaningless rather than differently signed.
Given the chart of accounts is as previous
Given postings are as previous
When report run : ReportSpec Vertical
| GroupBy      | Category   |
| From         | 2024-01-01 |
| To           | 2024-12-31 |
| Interval     | Whole      |
| QuickenSigns | true       |
Then report rows are : ReportRow
| Account                | Level | Amount   | IsSubtotal |
| Income                 | 0     | 42025.00 | true       |
| Income:Interest        | 1     | 25.00    | false      |
| Income:Salary          | 1     | 42000.00 | false      |
| Expenses               | 0     | -960.00  | true       |
| Expenses:Auto          | 1     | -450.00  | true       |
| Expenses:Auto:Fuel     | 2     | -150.00  | false      |
| Expenses:Auto:Repairs  | 2     | -300.00  | false      |
| Expenses:Groceries     | 1     | -500.00  | false      |
| Expenses:Uncategorized | 1     | -10.00   | false      |
Then report total is : ReportTotal Vertical
| TotalIncome   | 42025.00 |
| TotalExpenses | -960.00  |
| Net           | 41065.00 |
# Every figure is the one in the scenario above with the expense rows negated,
# and the net is unchanged at 41065.00.

