# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Investment activity
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

BusinessRule Income and expense arising inside an investment account is left out
Description A spending report answers what was earned and spent. A dividend
Description reinvested inside a retirement account was neither: no money
Description reached the household, and the figure is reported on a 1099
Description rather than budgeted against.
Details
Details So the test is not which category was used but where the money was.
Details A category posting counts when the transaction it belongs to touches
Details no investment account, and is left out when it touches one. The same
Details category can do both -- Invest Inc is real income when the dividend
Details lands in a bank account and is not when it stays in the brokerage --
Details which is why the category alone cannot decide it.
Details
Details Money actually moved out of an investment account into a bank account
Details is a transfer between two real accounts, so it never reached this
Details report in the first place; see the transfer scenario above.
Details
Details IncludeInvestmentActivity puts it all back, for the reader who wants
Details the whole picture rather than the household one.
Examples: InvestmentActivityCase
| TransactionTouches                     | Category          | Counts | Notes                               |
| A brokerage account only               | Income:Invest Inc | false  | A dividend reinvested; on the 1099  |
| A retirement account only              | Income:Invest Inc | false  | Same, and not yet taxable           |
| A brokerage account and a bank account | Income:Invest Inc | false  | The brokerage side taints it        |
| A bank account only                    | Income:Invest Inc | true   | A dividend paid out and spendable   |
| A brokerage account only               | Expenses:Fees     | false  | An advisory fee taken from the fund |
| A bank account only                    | Expenses:Fees     | true   | A fee paid by cheque                |

Attributes InvestmentActivityCase
| Attribute          | Type        | Default |
| TransactionTouches | String      |         |
| Category           | AccountPath |         |
| Counts             | Boolean     | false   |
| Notes              | String      | none    |

