Scenario A draw from another book does not reach the spending report
Description Money drawn from Ken Pugh, Inc. or WarpandByteDesigns is not income
Description here. That income was earned and already reported in the other
Description book, and counting it again would state the same earnings twice.
Description Entered as a transfer to an account for what that entity has paid
Description across, both sides are real, so nothing has to exclude it: only the
Description salary was earned in this book.
Details
Details The convention, rather than a mechanism. A draw is entered as this
Details transfer when it happens; nothing rewrites a category on import, and
Details the import stays a faithful mirror of its source. Twenty years of
Details history hold two such postings -- 27,500.00 drawn in December 2021
Details and 10,815.00 returned in August 2022 -- so a mapping in the importer
Details would be machinery for two lines, and a rule that applied only after
Details some cutover date would put a step in the middle of the multi-year
Details report that is the point of keeping the history at all.
Details
Details The reimbursement trees that carry the same two names are a different
Details thing and need nothing: a business expense paid personally debits a
Details subcategory and the reimbursement credits the parent, so the subtree
Details cancels itself. Over 2010 to 2026 the Warp And Byte tree nets 230.94
Details across 3,540 postings. What is left in such a net is a real personal
Details expense that was never reimbursed, so excluding it would be wrong.
Given the chart of accounts is : ChartOfAccounts
| Path                         | Type   | Placeholder |
| Assets:Ken~Checking          | Bank   | false       |
| Assets:Due~from~Ken~Pugh~Inc | Asset  | false       |
| Income                       | Income | true        |
| Income:Salary~Ken            | Income | false       |
Given postings are : PostingRow
| Ref | Date       | Payee                      | Account                      | Amount    |
| T1  | 2021-03-15 | Transfer from Ken Pugh Inc | Assets:Ken~Checking          | 27500.00  |
| T1  | 2021-03-15 | Transfer from Ken Pugh Inc | Assets:Due~from~Ken~Pugh~Inc | -27500.00 |
| T2  | 2021-03-31 | Acme Payroll               | Assets:Ken~Checking          | 1800.00   |
| T2  | 2021-03-31 | Acme Payroll               | Income:Salary~Ken            | -1800.00  |
When report run : ReportSpec Vertical
| GroupBy  | Category   |
| From     | 2021-01-01 |
| To       | 2021-12-31 |
| Interval | Whole      |
Then report rows are : ReportRow
| Account           | Level | Amount  | IsSubtotal |
| Income            | 0     | 1800.00 | true       |
| Income:Salary~Ken | 1     | 1800.00 | false      |
Then report total is : ReportTotal Vertical
| TotalIncome   | 1800.00 |
| TotalExpenses | 0.00    |
| Net           | 1800.00 |
# The 27,500.00 is absent, and the balance of Assets:Due from Ken Pugh Inc is
# where it can be read instead.

